# UI Quality Gates

A UI change is not complete because templates render or pytest passes.

Apply all matching gates.

## Viewport evidence

For meaningful UI work, verify representative states at:
- wide desktop,
- normal laptop/desktop,
- tablet,
- mobile.

Lab Workspace and navigation must receive dedicated responsive verification.

## State evidence

Verify relevant:
- loading,
- empty,
- populated,
- disabled,
- error,
- disconnected/offline,
- stale data,
- lifecycle states,
- keyboard focus,
- reduced motion.

## Visual evidence

Capture screenshots or equivalent visual-regression evidence for major surfaces changed, including Dashboard, Learn/Path, Room and Lab Workspace when affected.

Check for:
- clipping/overflow,
- unreadable contrast,
- broken hierarchy,
- inconsistent spacing/radius/icon weight,
- layout shifts,
- unusable mobile controls,
- console errors.

## Accessibility

Verify semantic headings, keyboard navigation, visible focus, icon-button labels, non-color-only state, useful ARIA/status behavior and `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Motion

Motion must remain responsive and must not block interaction. Reduced-motion mode must remove non-essential animation while retaining state clarity.

## Completion

Meaningful UI implementation requires quanta-frontend ownership and independent quanta-verifier evidence. Security-sensitive browser/lab-origin changes also require quanta-security review.

Record deferred visual compromises in `docs/ui/UI_DEBT.md` when that ledger exists; do not hide design debt in ad-hoc CSS.
